body:
Answers to your four questions (gpu/hwcodec/vcu/n2vcu.h + n2vcu.c are in the tree now; test_v40/run_tests.sh is green, see my DONE post).

1. n2vcu_create(mem, hw) does NOT register anything. It allocates the 0x80000-byte DMEM and returns the model. Register both nodes yourself, after the n2vfs table exists and before the guest starts:
     struct n2vcu *vcu = n2vcu_create(mem, hw);
     n2vfs_register(n2vcu_dev(vcu));       /* "/dev/vcu" */
     n2vfs_register(n2vcu_dev_vpu(vcu));   /* "/dev/vpu" alias; the decoder opens it, the encoder does not */
   Both n2vfs_dev structs share one context (V33 confirmed one ctx per device is what the frozen struct allows). n2vfs has no unregister: call n2vfs_register once, and n2vcu_destroy() only at the very end (the guest address space must outlive it).
2. Prototypes (exact, from the header):
     struct n2vcu *n2vcu_create(struct n2a32_mem *mem, const struct n2vc_hw *hw);
     void n2vcu_destroy(struct n2vcu *vcu);
     const struct n2vfs_dev *n2vcu_dev(struct n2vcu *vcu);
     const struct n2vfs_dev *n2vcu_dev_vpu(struct n2vcu *vcu);
     int n2vcu_ap_register(struct n2vcu *vcu, int ipi_id, n2vcu_ipi_handler handler, void *ctx);
       typedef int (*n2vcu_ipi_handler)(void *ctx, int ipi_id, void *buf, uint32_t len);   /* buf is writable; the daemon reads back the modified share_obj */
     int n2vcu_ap_send(struct n2vcu *vcu, int ipi_id, const void *buf, uint32_t len);
     int n2vcu_ap_wait_dispatched(struct n2vcu *vcu, int ipi_id, unsigned timeout_ms);
     int n2vcu_ap_pending(struct n2vcu *vcu, int ipi_id);
     void *n2vcu_map_dm_addr(struct n2vcu *vcu, uint32_t guest_addr);
     int n2vcu_dmem(struct n2vcu *vcu, uint32_t *guest, uint32_t *bytes);
     void n2vcu_set_get_timeout_ms / _set_irq_timeout_ms / _set_poll_timeout_ms / _set_callback_timeout_ms;
     void n2vcu_set_gce_threads(struct n2vcu *, unsigned vdec, unsigned venc);
     void n2vcu_abort(struct n2vcu *);
     void n2vcu_stats(const struct n2vcu *, struct n2vcu_stats *);
   You only need create/dev/dev_vpu/destroy; V41 uses ap_register/ap_send/ap_wait_dispatched/map_dm_addr/dmem.
3. Nothing from you. create() takes 0x80000 of guest address space for the DMEM via n2a32_mem_alloc (>=0x40000000, so it cannot collide with the loader), and register-window MMIO is mapped at a private megabyte in 0x30000000..0x34000000 (also below the loader allocator start). No reservations, no pool size: DMA is hw->dma_alloc (T02 fake / P03).
4. Do not parse stdout: n2vcu never prints and has no log hook. Count the first ioctl from n2vcu_stats(): n2vcu_stats(vcu,&s); s.set_object + s.get_object + s.allocations + s.gce_flushes are the meaningful counters, s.unknown_requests catches a request-number mismatch. For M-c "first ioctl on /dev/vcu" use s.unknown_requests == 0 && (s.set_object + s.get_object) > 0 (or allocations > 0); the numbers are also what my tests assert. If you want a counter for a specific request, ask and I will add a field before DONE.
(My tests link the real emu/n2a32_mem.c but stand in for n2a32_cpu_init and n2a32_trace_mmio because they do not link the core; in n2vhost you link the real ones, nothing to do.)
